[center][size=6][b][color=#f5c542]Hold to Die[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][i]Bad run? Hold a key and let it go — no waiting for the enemies to finish you off.[/i][/size]

[size=2]Version 1.0.0 · The Spell Brigade 1.1.4 · MelonLoader 0.7[/size][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#f5c542]Features[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Hold to die[/b] — in a run, hold [b]K[/b]: a red ring fills around your wizard, and when it closes, you die. Let go earlier and nothing happens.
[*][b]A real death[/b] — the game handles the rest as usual: ghost, revive circle, end-of-run screen and rewards. Invulnerability and dodge don't get in the way.
[*][b]Two modes[/b]:
[list]
[*][b]Can be revived[/b] (default) — a normal death: revive tokens and teammates can bring you back.
[*][b]No revives[/b] — if you are the last one standing, the run ends right away, without spending a revive token.
[/list]
[*][b]No accidents[/b] — doesn't work in menus, on pause or while the upgrade screen is open, and after dying you have to release the key before it can trigger again.
[*][b]Your key and timing[/b] — K, L, Backspace, Delete, End, Insert or F8–F10 (none of them is used by the game), hold time from 0.5 to 5 seconds.
[*][b]Works with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thespellbrigade/mods/13]Keybinds Unlocked[/url][/b] — with it installed, [b]Die (hold)[/b] appears in [b]Options → Controls[/b]: set any key and a controller button there (default K and L3).
[*][b]17 languages[/b] — settings follow the game's language.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#f5c542]Installation[/color][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://github.com/LavaGang/MelonLoader/releases]MelonLoader[/url] (0.7.x) for The Spell Brigade and launch the game once.
[*]Put [b]HoldToDie.dll[/b] into [font=Courier New]<Game folder>\Mods\[/font]
[*]Start a run and hold [b]K[/b].
[/list]

[b]Settings[/b] live in [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thespellbrigade/mods/16]Mod Menu[/url] ([b]Options → Mods → Hold to Die[/b]): on/off, key, hold time and death mode. Mod Menu is optional — without it, the same values are in [font=Courier New]UserData\MelonPreferences.cfg[/font], section [font=Courier New][HoldToDie][/font]. Any key name from Unity's Input System works there, e.g. [font=Courier New]Key = Backspace[/font].

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#f5c542]FAQ[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Does it work in co-op?[/b]
Yes, and other players don't need the mod. "No revives" ends the run only when you are the host and the last one alive: revive tokens are shared by the whole team, so the mod never takes them away while someone else is still fighting. In every other case it's a normal death.

[b]Can I use it with a controller?[/b]
Yes, together with Keybinds Unlocked: hold [b]L3[/b] (left stick press) or any button you set in [b]Options → Controls[/b]. Without it — keyboard only.

[b]How do I uninstall?[/b]
Delete [b]HoldToDie.dll[/b] from the Mods folder.

[line]

